{
 "summary": "Optimizes the `deterministic-fuzz-coverage` developer tool by comparing merged `.profdata` profile files directly between runs and skipping expensive `llvm-cov show` report rendering when profiles match. If profile data differs, the tool falls back to rendering and diffing coverage reports to pinpoint non-determinism. It also switches the parallelism argument from positional to `--parallelism=<value>`.",
 "problem": "Generating human-readable `llvm-cov show` coverage reports for every fuzz input across two separate runs dominates the runtime of fuzz coverage determinism checks, even though almost all inputs produce identical reports that are discarded.",
 "evidence": [
  "Author benchmarks showing a ~3x speedup on qa-assets corpora: `addition_overflow` dropped from 32s to 10s, and `process_message` dropped from 719s to 247s (PR description).",
  "On `process_message`, all 2,386 inputs took the fast path, eliminating 4,772 `llvm-cov show` report invocations (PR description)."
 ],
